k memory for numbers, nasty remarks, pretentious, wrong tone, grumpy, uncooperative. Both have crew cooperation issues. Which is more severe? Hard to say. But D's strengths directly address decision quality and responsibility, which are critical. So we might shift to D.\n\nThus as Agent 3, we can say we now align with D, given the evidence. Provide vote D.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 2's and Agent 1's points, and mention explicit facts: D takes responsibility seriously, solves problems extremely well, concentrates very well, responds adequately to unexpected events. Also mention D's concerns: arrogance, hot temper, weak leadership, moody, loner. Compare to B's weak memory for numbers and nasty remarks. Conclude D is stronger.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote D.\n\nProceed."}
